Now my daughters (the LegoHack DevTeam) all have their own computers,
they've discovered Falcon's Eye which comes with their SuSE
installation. All by themselves. I think one of the eight-year-olds
found it first and told her sisters. They're discovering things and
having tremendous fun.

The advantage of FE, for Dutch-speaking eight- and ten-year-olds, is
that it doesn't require them to be able to spell English words, and
that they can discover a lot by trial and error.

I'll keep the group posted about spectacular successes (and probably
spectacular failures as well).

